# EventGenie AI – Environment Variables Example
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your values.
# NEVER commit `.env.local` or any file containing real keys to version control.
# The app is fully functional WITHOUT a Gemini key (offline fallback engine).

# ─── Optional: Gemini AI Integration ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Obtain a free key at: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# Leave blank to use the local deterministic offline engine.
# This key is pasted into the UI form at runtime and is NEVER stored server-side.
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# ─── App Configuration (Optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public base URL for Vercel/Netlify deployments
VITE_APP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5173

# ─── Notes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# - All VITE_ prefixed variables are bundled into the client-side JS.
# - Do NOT put private server-side secrets in VITE_ variables.
# - The Gemini key is handled via a UI input field (not environment variable)
#   to ensure zero accidental exposure in CI/CD logs or build artifacts.
